5,1,1,talk,Shizue,,"Good morning, everyone. Before we rank these proposals, I’d like to understand what actually happened to our past awards.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Shizue"",""self"":true,""raw"":""**Shizue**: Good morning, everyone. Before we rank these proposals, I’d like to understand what actually happened to our past awards.""}]}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We should verify the current staffing levels before committing to any long-term projects.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I’m concerned about the capacity of our shared facilities. We need to know if the infrastructure can support the proposed workloads.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m curious why the headline grant size stays constant while the actual purchasing power seems to shift unpredictably across different budget lines.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,I worry about how often past projects lost time to administrative delays rather than the science itself.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that purchasing power point is vital. I’d like to check the closeout files of finished awards to see what actually delivered.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Ryuji, I want to check the staffing rolls for technical posts to see who is actually available.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Victoria, I want to check the incident logs on shared instrumentation to see if our equipment is reliable enough.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Benjamin, I want to check the travel and bench-fee lines in the ledgers to see where the money actually goes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Midori, I want to check the portfolio review of schedule overruns to see where delays actually happen.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, I also need to review the portfolio review of schedule overruns to see where delays actually happen.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Ryuji, I also need to review the minutes on secondments and crew strength to understand who is actually available.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Victoria, I also need to check the accreditation and bookings at shared facilities to see if we have the capacity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Benjamin, I also need to check the national computing agreement and facility day rates to see which costs are absorbed centrally.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,"@Midori, I also need to check the national repository deposit turnaround to see if data release delays are a real bottleneck.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Shizue,,I believe we have covered our essential checks. Let us proceed to the next stage with the information we have gathered.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed. The data will clarify our constraints. Let us review the findings before making any final judgments.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Victoria,,Agreed. We must ensure our infrastructure can support the chosen project before we commit.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. Let’s see what the ledgers and agreements actually reveal about our real constraints.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,Agreed. I hope the data helps us avoid repeating past administrative mistakes. Let’s see what we found.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
